{"comment_text": {"ja25:0.1": "", "ja25:0.2": "", "ja25:0.3": "", "ja25:0.4": "", "ja25:1.1": "When a fussy horse refuses to drink at one ford, the canny keeper realizes he needs to be taken somewhere else. ", "ja25:1.2": "", "ja25:1.3": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Accāsana</i> is <i lang='pi' translate='no'>ati</i> + <i lang='pi' translate='no'>asana</i>, “over-eat”. ", "ja25:1.4": "", "ja25:2.1": ""}, "html_text": {"ja25:0.1": "<article id='ja25'><header><ul><li class='division'>{}</li>", "ja25:0.2": "<li>{}</li>", "ja25:0.3": "<li>{}</li></ul>", "ja25:0.4": "<h1 class='sutta-title'>{}</h1></header>", "ja25:1.1": "<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja25:1.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja25:1.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja25:1.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p></blockquote>", "ja25:2.1": "<p class='endsutta'>{}</p></article>"}, "root_text": {"ja25:0.1": "Jātaka ", "ja25:0.2": "Ekakanipāta ", "ja25:0.3": "Kuruṅgavagga ", "ja25:0.4": "5. Titthajātaka ", "ja25:1.1": "“Aññamaññehi titthehi, ", "ja25:1.2": "assaṁ pāyehi sārathi; ", "ja25:1.3": "Accāsanassa puriso, ", "ja25:1.4": "pāyāsassapi tappatī”ti. ", "ja25:2.1": "Titthajātakaṁ pañcamaṁ. "}, "translation_text": {"ja25:0.1": "Stories of Past Lives 25 ", "ja25:0.2": "The Book of the Ones ", "ja25:0.3": "The Four-horned Antelope ", "ja25:0.4": "Fords: a past life story ", "ja25:1.1": "At one ford or another ", "ja25:1.2": "lead the horse to drink, rider. ", "ja25:1.3": "For man who overeats, ", "ja25:1.4": "even milk-rice is a torment. ", "ja25:2.1": ""}, "reference_text": {"ja25:0.1": "", "ja25:0.2": "", "ja25:0.3": "", "ja25:0.4": "", "ja25:1.1": "csp1ed22.7, csp2ed22.7, dr27.10, ms22J_54, msdiv25, pts-vp-pli1.185, sya27.9", "ja25:1.2": "", "ja25:1.3": "", "ja25:1.4": "", "ja25:2.1": "ms22J_55"}, "keys_order": ["ja25:0.1", "ja25:0.2", "ja25:0.3", "ja25:0.4", "ja25:1.1", "ja25:1.2", "ja25:1.3", "ja25:1.4", "ja25:2.1"]}